      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "WOLF JUNIOR (2) won by a short head last start despite having a case of the thumps, which augurs well for another race 9 days later. His record here over the trip is strong, and he can go back-to-back. SH'BOURNE POWER (1) got back after missing the kick again last start and then failed to run on wide out off a slow tempo. He will have Craig Newitt in the saddle this time, and with a better beginning, he can have a say in the finish of this race. Stick with him. DUBAI AFFAIR (4) won a trial prior to a modest effort off a wide gate when resuming here 3 weeks ago. She gets a big swing in her draw this time, strips fitter, and with the blinkers off, she can finish a lot closer. WITHIN SIGHT (5) has raced her way back into some good form again, finishing runner-up in her last 2 starts. She is likely to produce another honest effort in this. TROTSKY (7) got in the final stride to score by a nose here 4 weeks ago and can be competitive again. Include in all top 4 combos again.",
